        "original_id": "2c19cf5d-583f-5e5b-a1dd-81a696917ef6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Panther terminology\n- Animals: Cougar, Jaguar, Leopard\n- Taxonomy: Panthera, big cats\n\nFacts:\n- In some parts of North America, the term \"panther\" is used to mean the Cougar (Puma concolor).\n- In South America, the term \"panther\" is used to mean the Jaguar (Panthera onca).\n- Elsewhere, the term \"panther\" refers to the Leopard (Panthera pardus).\n- The Leopard (Panthera pardus) is one of the five big cats in the genus Panthera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
